<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What is a Double Currency Net Worth Certificate?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>A double currency net worth certificate is a CA-certified financial statement presenting total assets, liabilities, and net worth in two currencies simultaneously - Indian Rupees and a specified foreign currency - using the RBI reference exchange rate on the certification date, authenticated with an 18-digit UDIN from ICAI.</p><p>The certificate contains parallel columns showing every asset and liability in both INR and the target currency. Movable assets (bank balances, FDs, mutual funds, shares, gold, vehicles), immovable assets (property at Ready Reckoner rate), and all liabilities are individually converted. The conversion rate, source (RBI reference rate), and date are explicitly stated.</p><p>For Mumbai visa applicants, this allows the embassy officer to assess financial capacity directly in the destination currency without manual conversion. A Canada Express Entry applicant submitting INR + CAD enables the visa officer to immediately assess IRCC proof-of-funds thresholds. Patron uses only the official RBI reference rate - never Google/market/bank rates. Coordinate with <a href="/statutory-audit">Statutory Audit</a> and <a href="/gst-returns">GST Returns</a>.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Double Currency Net Worth Certificate in Mumbai:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>RBI Reference Rate:</strong> Official daily rate at rbi.org.in. Direct for USD/GBP/EUR/JPY. Cross-rate for CAD/AUD/SGD/NZD/AED. The only acceptable conversion rate</li><li><strong>UDIN:</strong> 18-digit ICAI number mandatory since 2019. Embassies, RBI, SEBI verify on udin.icai.org</li><li><strong>Ready Reckoner Rate:</strong> Maharashtra government annual property valuation for stamp duty. Standard for Mumbai net worth</li><li><strong>Proof of Funds (POF):</strong> Immigration threshold - Canada IRCC specifies minimum in CAD by family size</li><li><strong>Family Net Worth:</strong> Combined applicant + family (spouse/parents) for student visa sponsorship</li><li><strong>Cross-Rate:</strong> For currencies without direct RBI rate, derived via USD cross-rate</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
