            <h2 class="section-title">Double Currency Net Worth Certificate - Legal Framework</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>ICAI UDIN:</strong> Mandatory 18-digit number for all CA certificates since 2019. <a href="https://udin.icai.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">udin.icai.org</a>. Embassies, RBI, SEBI verify before accepting.</p><p><strong>Chartered Accountants Act, 1949:</strong> Only CA with valid COP can issue. No other professional authorised.</p><p><strong>RBI Reference Rate:</strong> Published daily at <a href="https://rbi.org.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">rbi.org.in</a>. Direct rates: USD, GBP, EUR, JPY. Cross-rates: CAD, AUD, SGD, NZD, AED. Only acceptable conversion rate.</p><p><strong>Maharashtra Ready Reckoner Rates:</strong> Annual Statement of Rates by Inspector General of Registration. Standard Mumbai property valuation for CA certificates.</p><p><strong>FEMA, 1999:</strong> Dual-currency net worth supports FEMA compliance for LRS declarations and overseas investment.</p><p><strong>Consequences:</strong> Using non-RBI rate = professional misrepresentation. Embassy may reject visa. CA faces ICAI disciplinary action. Inflated net worth = Section 420 IPC if discovered.</p>

